Every ACPI table QEMU 11.1.0 published to a Profile::Headless guest, read out
of guest physical memory over QMP `human-monitor-command` `xp/Nxb <addr>` — the
host's read of the guest's memory, so no byte here came through the decoder
these fixtures judge.

The RSDP's address is the one value taken from the guest (the kernel's
`ACPI: RSDP at` line); every other address was walked host-side out of these
bytes, and the signature and checksum of what came back are what say it was
right. Each table sums to zero.

  rsdp.bin  0x7fb7e014      xsdt.bin  0x7fb7d0e8
  facp.bin  0x7fb79000      apic.bin  0x7fb78000
  hpet.bin  0x7fb77000      mcfg.bin  0x7fb76000
  dmar.bin  0x7fb75000      waet.bin  0x7fb74000

The addresses are `tests/fixtures.rs`'s `REGIONS`, so the XSDT's own entries
point at them and the walk under test is the real one. The DSDT this boot named
(0x7fb7a000, 8500 bytes) is not here: nothing in this crate decodes one.
